  "fnthinkConsentRevokeMsg": "After revoking, these stop working on this device: anything that goes through the server (the receive loop stops on its next round), remote control, creating/rotating/revoking ingress endpoints, starting and approving pairings, creating/enabling a Fnthink channel and \"send one\", and the test that carries a body. Nothing is deleted - the peer list, endpoints, channel configs, message history and pairing records all stay. Turning them back on needs a fresh consent tap (the full text stays readable first).",
